# ---------------- Abstract ----------------
H('Abstract')
AB1="The mobilised colistin resistance ("
AB2=") gene families encode phosphoethanolamine transferases that are structurally and functionally equivalent to chromosomal EptA. Where each family came from, and which chromosomal genes might be recruited next, remain only partly resolved. We assembled 191 proteins, comprising 150 chromosomal transferases retrieved from RefSeq across 44 genera of "
AB3=" and of taxa implicated as donors, 28 unclustered records from UniProtKB, the reference allele of every named "
AB4=(" family that has a reference allele in the catalogue, eleven of the twelve named to date, and five members of the wider alkaline phosphatase superfamily, four of them used to root the tree, less three records that proved to be exact duplicates. Maximum-likelihood inference under a selected model placed the mobilised proteins in nine separate lineages of the EptA clade in the primary analysis of 161 sequences, and in ten when the unclustered records were added and the tree was rooted on the outgroup. A constrained tree enforcing their monophyly was rejected by the approximately unbiased test at p = {pau}, so a single origin can be excluded and the topologies place the number of separate capture events at nine or ten. Unclustered searching identified closer chromosomal relatives than clustered searching had, by as much as 36 percentage points, and two chromosomal records proved identical to catalogued alleles over their full length, one in ").format(pau='8.1 x 10-6')
AB5=" and one in "
AB6=(". Six positions of the catalytic apparatus were invariant across every sequence examined, and the ten that vary were reconstructed at the node each mobilised lineage shares with its chromosomal relatives, where the six disulfide-forming cysteines, Lys333 and His478 were recovered with posterior probability 1.00 at all nine nodes. Synonymous sites were saturated between families, with dS above one in {a} of {b} comparisons, so selection was assessed within families, where the ratio of non-synonymous to synonymous change ran from 0.08 to 0.64. Profile searches built from catalogued alleles reached only three of 178 chromosomal and related proteins, all of them at least 95% identical to an allele of a well-catalogued family, and missed proteins 80% to 90% identical as well as one identical to MCR-6.1. The enzymes were complete before mobilisation. What changed was their genomic setting, and a pool of near-identical chromosomal genes sits beyond the reach of reference-based surveillance.").format(a=S['n_dS_gt1'],b=S['n_pairs'])
