# ---------------- Discussion ----------------
H('4. Discussion')
RICH([('The mobilised families do not share an origin. They occupy the clade that also holds chromosomal EptA, but within it they sit among chromosomal sequences from taxa that are not closely related to one another, and a tree that forces them together is rejected by every test we applied. Nine lineages were recovered, which sets a floor rather than a count: families whose donors have not been sequenced will appear more isolated than they are, and two chromosomal records identical to catalogued alleles show how much of the relevant diversity is still undescribed. Moraxellaceae, ',False),('Shewanella',True),(', ',False),('Aeromonas',True),(', ',False),('Cupriavidus',True),(' and ',False),('Buttiauxella',True),(' each account for at least one event. The pattern is of a gene function repeatedly captured from whichever genome happened to be nearby, not of one ancestral resistance gene spreading.',False)])
P('The catalytic apparatus supports that reading directly. Six positions are occupied identically in every protein examined, mobilised or not, which tells us only that the superfamily constrains them. Eight of the ten positions that vary are informative about mobilisation, and at the stem node of every mobilised lineage all eight are reconstructed with a posterior probability of 1.00. The remaining two, Ser284 and Asn329, are reconstructed in the chromosomal configuration at six of the nine nodes, as serine and asparagine at the node leading to MCR-1, MCR-2 and MCR-6, and in two further configurations at the nodes leading to MCR-12 and MCR-5, which is what makes the result a finding rather than a restatement of the alignment. Nothing suggests that the transition from chromosome to plasmid required a change in the enzyme. What the donor already did, the mobilised gene continued to do.')
RICH([('Where the transition shows is in the flanking DNA. Three of the six informative deposits place a transposase or an insertion sequence within a few kilobases of the mobilised gene, and the other three place it on a plasmid backbone among replication and transfer functions. The ISApl1 arrangement around ',False),('mcr-1',True),(' is the clearest and is consistent with the transposition model proposed for Tn6330 (Snesrud et al., 2016, 2018; Poirel, Kieffer, and Nordmann, 2017). No transposase was found within about 10 kb of the four chromosomal loci we examined, but we draw no conclusion from that. Composite transposons are routinely identified using windows three to five times wider, and a negative result at 10 kb does not exclude an element at 25 kb. The comparison between mobilised and chromosomal contexts in this paper is therefore suggestive and not conclusive.',False)])
RICH([('The identity values distribute in a way that is informative about timing, once the artefacts are removed. MCR-1 differs from a chromosomal ',False),('Moraxella',True),(' protein by 1.3%, MCR-3 from a chromosomal ',False),('Aeromonas media',True),(' protein by 5.0%, and MCR-5 and MCR-6 have chromosomal counterparts that are identical to them. Those events are recent on any reading. MCR-9 and MCR-10 are 87.4% and 84.6% identical to their closest counterpart in ',False),('B. cochleicola',True),(', which places them further back. MCR-8 and MCR-12, at 43.8% and 40.6%, either come from lineages that have not been sampled or are older than the rest. A 400-residue partial protein of ',False),('C. freundii',True),(' is 99.0% identical to MCR-9.1 over the region it covers, but a value measured on a fragment is not comparable with one measured on a whole protein, and the recency of the ',False),('mcr-9',True),(' event should not be judged from it.',False)])
RICH([('The practical implication concerns surveillance, and it is now supported by a test rather than by assertion. A reference-based search using the most permissive threshold compatible with family boundaries reached three of the 178 chromosomal and related proteins, and all three were at least 95% identical to an allele of a well-catalogued family. Everything below that was missed, including a protein 87.4% identical to MCR-9.1. The sharpest case is A0A220T317 of ',False),('Moraxella',True),(' sp. MSG47C17, which is identical to MCR-6.1 residue for residue and was not detected, because ',False),('mcr-6',True),(' has two catalogued alleles and cannot be modelled as a family at all. Detection failure here is therefore not only a matter of divergence but of how unevenly the families are catalogued. A survey that asks which genomes carry a known ',False),('mcr',True),(' allele is unlikely to return a signal from a genome carrying a gene that a future family will be named after, and profile-based searching at the level of the family, rather than the allele, would narrow that gap at the cost of a specificity problem that would have to be managed.',False)])
RICH([('Just under a quarter of the chromosomal transferases in this dataset turned out to act on osmoregulated periplasmic glucans rather than on lipopolysaccharide. That distinction was not visible in the annotation of the records, which describe most of them simply as phosphoethanolamine transferases or sulfatase-family proteins, and it matters for anyone using annotation alone to estimate how many potential colistin resistance genes a genome carries. Counts made that way will be inflated. The ',False),('opgE',True),('-like proteins belong to the same superfamily and share the catalytic residues, but they have a different substrate and there is no evidence that any of them confers resistance.',False)])
P('Several limitations apply. Retrieval used one representative per cluster per genus, and although the identity analyses were repeated without clustering for the implicated donor genera, the wider dataset remains a sample rather than a census. The deep nodes of the tree are weakly supported, which is usual for a family this divergent, and the conclusion that mobilisation happened repeatedly rests on the topology test rather than on those nodes. Synonymous sites are saturated between families, so nothing can be said about the strength of selection during the transfer events themselves. Genomic context could be examined for only a small number of loci, and the window was narrow. Several of the sequences in the closest-relative table come from draft assemblies and metagenome-assembled genomes, where the distinction between a chromosomal and a plasmid location is not always reliable.')

